    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "The idea that releasing the struggle is \"courageous\" is an interesting inversion of everything we're typically taught. It suggests that the most rational response to an unsolvable problem isn't to struggle against it, but to conclude it. In your view, does that mean there comes a point where continuing to exist is actually an irrational act?",
